Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.01,0:00:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.73,0:00:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Burning Knuckle Strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.79,0:00:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Big Bang Dragon Ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.29,0:00:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.20,0:00:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's up to you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.55,0:00:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Save Mai.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.05,0:00:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Valon!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.41,0:00:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what, Mai?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.77,0:00:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as that Oricalkos thing\Nhas control over your mind,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.87,0:00:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll never be able to talk any\Nsense into you The only way
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.27,0:00:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I can save you at this point\Nis to duel you If you say so,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.31,0:00:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,My move, the seal of Oricalkos.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.67,0:00:42.47,Default,,0,0,0,,We're both locked in the seal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.73,0:00:46.43,Default,,0,0,0,,and only one of us will escape\NI don't plan on running away,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.51,0:00:49.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna keep fighting until\NI break through to you, Mai,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.83,0:00:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,or lose my soul trying
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.75,0:00:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, oh,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.66,0:01:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,oh,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.71,0:01:24.54,Default,,0,0,0,,oh, oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.89,0:01:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta find him!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.09,0:02:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.00,0:02:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you, man?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.27,0:02:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you down there?\NJoey! Answer us! Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.53,0:02:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I could swear that Urikalkos thing\Nactivated right here! Me too!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.31,0:02:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,So why isn't it here now?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.13,0:02:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless we're too late!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.77,0:02:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't say that, Taya!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.77,0:02:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang in there, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.17,0:02:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Seto!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.08,0:02:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.73,0:02:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,It's simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.83,0:02:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We exterminate these\Noversized cockroaches.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.85,0:02:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Blue eyes, come forth!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.75,0:02:42.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Eliminate this pest problem\Nwith white lightning strikes!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.75,0:02:50.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man, how are you supposed\Nto get rid of these things?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.95,0:02:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,When you smash them, they come right back.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.87,0:02:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Moguba, what do I always tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.09,0:03:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,If at first you don't succeed, blast\Nthem with your blue eyes again!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.69,0:03:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Seto, help! Hey! Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.03,0:03:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I play Critias!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.03,0:03:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, bro.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.89,0:03:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,But they're not gone yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Those goons won't give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.27,0:03:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, then, I won't either.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.69,0:03:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Dragons, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.95,0:03:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong, Wheeler?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.65,0:03:44.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Are my harpies too much to handle?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.07,0:03:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you try fighting\Ntwo duels in a row?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.65,0:03:49.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Boo-hoo.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.01,0:03:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit making excuses and duel,\Nor you'll end up like Ballad.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.25,0:03:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, I really miss the old my.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.57,0:04:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon my Swordsman of\NLandstar in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.21,0:04:04.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm shaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.07,0:04:06.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well, you should be.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.75,0:04:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I'm not done.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.81,0:04:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I place two cards face\Ndown and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.99,0:04:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm in worse shape than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.37,0:04:20.53,Default,,0,0,0,,That last duel wiped me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.43,0:04:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's not over yet. So you brag\Nabout your new monster and then end your
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.51,0:04:43.11,Default,,0,0,0,,turn without using it how lame i'm just\Nwaiting for the right time that is so
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.19,0:04:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,typical wheeler you put on this tough guy\Nshow for everyone when deep down you're
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.99,0:04:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,nothing but a scared little kid Do you\Nhonestly think you can win this duel?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.91,0:04:54.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That depends.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.59,0:04:56.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Depends on what?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.95,0:05:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It depends on what you mean\Nwhen you say the word win.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.11,0:05:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Cause to me, winning's about\Nmore than cards and life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.65,0:05:05.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, spare me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.45,0:05:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,When I first met you, you told me\Nall you cared about was yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.11,0:05:12.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You also said because of\Nthat you had no friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.65,0:05:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,But we told you you\Nshould hang out with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.65,0:05:18.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And after we fought side by side,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.65,0:05:22.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you found something\Nmore important than winning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.11,0:05:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,A little something called friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.83,0:05:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,But I guess I was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.59,0:05:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe you just forgot.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.23,0:05:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, save it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.83,0:05:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I've come way too far to turn back now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.03,0:05:36.19,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Mai...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.27,0:05:38.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I've had enough of your lecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.93,0:05:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to destroy you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.81,0:05:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You're mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.43,0:05:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, Mai...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.63,0:05:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Just know, I'll always stand\Nby you, no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.11,0:05:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll never forget\Nour friendship. Now go!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.79,0:05:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I will!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.77,0:05:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You're done!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.71,0:05:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Cyber Harpy, attack his\Nswordsman of Landstar!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.75,0:06:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.09,0:06:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Reveal face-down card!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.21,0:06:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,My double magical arm vine!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.13,0:06:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,This card allows me to\Nsacrifice two of my own monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.59,0:06:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to gain control\Nof two of your monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.59,0:06:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I still have two Cyber Harpies\Nleft, so ladies, do your thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.07,0:06:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, I'm not done yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.21,0:06:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I reveal my trap card,\Nknown as Vow of Tribe!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.05,0:06:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as this card's in effect,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.13,0:06:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,if the same monsters are standing on both\Nsides of the field, they can't attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.85,0:06:37.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And since two of your Cyber\NHarpies belong to me at the moment,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.43,0:06:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,that means all six of them are useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.63,0:06:41.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Now what do you say to that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.21,0:06:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, nice move.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.15,0:06:44.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean that, Mai?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.87,0:06:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I wouldn't be this\Ngood a duelist without you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.43,0:06:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You've always pushed me to be my best.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.99,0:06:53.65,Default,,0,0,0,,How can he still feel that way about me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.91,0:06:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,After everything I put him through,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.05,0:06:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,why doesn't he give into his\Nanger like everyone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.35,0:07:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I could never be like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.79,0:07:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe Wheeler really is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.21,0:07:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought if I won, I could make\Nyou forget about Joey Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.03,0:07:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,But now I understand why\Nhe meant so much to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.15,0:07:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,The guy's got heart
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.41,0:07:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.32,0:07:21.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm fighting you with all my heart and\Nsoul. It's the only way to save you. So,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.35,0:07:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe Valon was right. That just gives\Nme all the more reason to crush Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.29,0:07:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,And if he really duels with all his soul,\Nthen I'll just have to take his soul away.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.39,0:07:35.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all over for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.23,0:07:50.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It won't be long now. Great Leviathan,\Nsoon the chosen duelists will be ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.13,0:07:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,your move wheeler your last\Nmove she may not admit it but
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.13,0:08:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,my can't fool me i know deep\Ndown she values our friendship i
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.55,0:08:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,just have to remind her because\Nwe've been through way too much
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.53,0:08:12.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Together and I won't let her\Nthrow that away. I'm not done yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.81,0:08:19.15,Default,,0,0,0,,i think i'll sacrifice the two cyber\Nhobbies i got from you plus my swordsman
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.23,0:08:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,of landstar what are you up to wheeler\Nnow meet guilford the lightning
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.51,0:08:37.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever Guilford the\NLightning is summoned
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.73,0:08:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,to the field by\Nsacrificing three monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.31,0:08:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It destroys every monster on my\Nopponent's side. Guilford, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.95,0:08:55.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's time for my Guilford to\Nattack your life points directly
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.51,0:09:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,See that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.87,0:09:13.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey Wheeler's got plenty\Nof fight left in him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.47,0:09:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That may be. But do you have enough?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.33,0:09:26.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I doubt it. Besides,\NWheeler, it's my turn now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.59,0:09:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,For starters, I'll play this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.33,0:09:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The card of sanctity.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.29,0:09:37.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now both players have to draw until\Nwe each have six cards in our head.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.97,0:09:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,So that means you draw\Ntoo, Brainiac. Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.99,0:09:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, draw anything worth using?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.87,0:09:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess you'll have to\Nwait and see, won't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.63,0:09:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't draw hammos,\Nbut these should help.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.19,0:09:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, time to make my move, whether\Nhe drew his legendary dragon or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.63,0:10:06.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate the magic card, Monster\NReborn, to bring back my Cyber Harpy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.51,0:10:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,But one's never enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.37,0:10:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,So next I'll activate my Elegant Egotist.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.71,0:10:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This magic card multiplies\Nmy Cyber Harpy by three.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.59,0:10:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, how many harpies do\Nyou have in that deck?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.37,0:10:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoo-hoo, you might want\Nto pay attention to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.89,0:10:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate one more magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.77,0:10:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Harpy Lady Phoenix Formation!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.15,0:10:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Since I have three harpies on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.03,0:10:47.73,Default,,0,0,0,,this card destroys up to\Nthree of your monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.81,0:10:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And once your pathetic\Ncreatures are history,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.71,0:10:55.15,Default,,0,0,0,,the total number of their attack points\Ngets subtracted from your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.23,0:10:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And now take this!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.93,0:11:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,One more attack and this duel's over!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.67,0:11:55.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The Claw of Hamos.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.71,0:11:57.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, are you a sight for sore eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.47,0:12:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll activate my\N"Warrior Returning Alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.57,0:12:07.03,Default,,0,0,0,,This card allows me to transfer a Warrior\Nfrom the graveyard back to my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.11,0:12:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose my Blue Flame Swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.83,0:12:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I think I'll lay this\Nlittle magic card on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.27,0:12:18.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It's called Dark Dragon Ritual!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.65,0:12:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Ladies and gents,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.17,0:12:26.52,Default,,0,0,0,,sit back and enjoy the show as I make\NGear Free the Iron Knight disappear!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.49,0:12:31.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Then watch as my Night of Dark\NDragons suddenly materializes!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.53,0:12:34.59,Default,,0,0,0,,But my trick's not over yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.07,0:12:36.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, with a flick of my wrists,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.81,0:12:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make this new monster\Ndisappear before your very eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.09,0:12:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Letting me conjure up\Nsomething even more powerful!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.51,0:12:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,How about a warm welcome\Nfor my red-eyes, Black Drip?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.07,0:12:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you're so hot, but too bad\Nyour red-eyes can't attack this turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.75,0:12:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.33,0:13:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I got something else I'm\Nplanning to attack you with now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.11,0:13:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The Claw of Hamos!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.57,0:13:09.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But before I attack,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.45,0:13:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll combine my Hamos with my Red Eyes\Nto form Red Eyes Black Dragon Sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.87,0:13:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The perfect weapon for my swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.03,0:13:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Now he's even stronger\NBlue Flame Swordsman,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.11,0:13:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack a Cyber Harpy\Nwith your Dragon Sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.85,0:13:34.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll place two cards face\Ndown, and it's back to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.57,0:13:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got to pull through this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.33,0:13:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.33,0:13:45.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad, dork.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.15,0:13:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But your flame swordsman is only as\Nstrong as his weapon, right? So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.93,0:13:54.01,Default,,0,0,0,,So this card's going to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.23,0:13:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Harpy's Feather Duster!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.47,0:14:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Now his flame swordsman\Nis defenseless against my
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.59,0:14:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Harpies! And his life points\Nare wide open to an attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.75,0:14:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to blast him out of my life forever
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.61,0:14:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Activate spell reproduction
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.25,0:14:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all I have to do is get\Nrid of two magic cards from my
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.53,0:14:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,hand And I can bring back another\Nmagic card from my graveyard
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.69,0:14:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Like this
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.19,0:14:29.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You're about to play your\NPhoenix formation, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.43,0:14:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,So what are you waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.23,0:14:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.14,0:14:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You're absolutely right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.41,0:14:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna finish you off\Nwith a little Phoenix action.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.33,0:14:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now your Swordsman's attack points\Nget subtracted from your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.31,0:14:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.22,0:14:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,But why didn't you lose any points?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.09,0:14:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I did tell you about Flame\NSwordsman's special effect, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.69,0:14:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I can automatically\Ntransfer his attack points
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.25,0:14:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,to any other monster on\Nthe field that I choose,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.71,0:14:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,so...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.62,0:14:59.24,Default,,0,0,0,,So you chose to give him to my harpy?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.51,0:15:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep, all his points are hers.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.47,0:15:05.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I reduced my\Nswordsman's strength to zero,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.51,0:15:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't lose any life\Npoints when you zapped him.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.97,0:15:10.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, whenever Blue Flame\NSwordsman is destroyed,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.85,0:15:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I can summon the original\NFlame Swordsman in his place.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.83,0:15:15.77,Default,,0,0,0,,But remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.99,0:15:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,you have the strongest monster now, and\Nhow you use it is completely up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.89,0:15:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But like I said before, you're one\Nof the greatest duelists I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.97,0:15:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm sure you're going\Nto make the right decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.11,0:15:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Because my, underneath all that anger\Nand frustration, is a good person.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.49,0:15:35.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.75,0:15:36.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.09,0:15:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And by the way, good luck out there today.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.37,0:15:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,That was a long time ago, and I'm\Nsick of taking back seat to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.61,0:15:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry you felt that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.11,0:15:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,But you think you're any better off now?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.31,0:15:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You're still taking a back seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.55,0:15:57.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Only now it's to some loony\Nwho promised you power.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.01,0:16:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Without power, I'm nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.71,0:16:03.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Mai.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.39,0:16:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.75,0:16:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too late now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.55,0:16:09.59,Default,,0,0,0,,My fate's already been sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.91,0:16:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And so has yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.35,0:16:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Mai move. Here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.05,0:16:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,i'll place one card face down on the field
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.57,0:16:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,now i'm done so give me your best shot
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.51,0:16:36.23,Default,,0,0,0,,let's end this right now cyber\Nharpy destroy his flame swordsman
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.31,0:16:40.19,Default,,0,0,0,,with your virtual slash attack And\Nwipe out Wheeler's life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.07,0:16:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.03,0:16:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Reveal my face down card!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.07,0:16:45.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Skull dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.69,0:16:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to lower your\Nmonster's attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.01,0:16:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like your cyber-harpy's\Nstrength just got cut in half.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.01,0:17:00.36,Default,,0,0,0,,He's still stronger than your swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.95,0:17:06.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And now to wipe out the\Nrest of your life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.11,0:17:09.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Cyber Harpy!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.39,0:17:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack his!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.05,0:17:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.13,0:17:15.43,Default,,0,0,0,,That's my problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.33,0:17:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a no-brainer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.15,0:17:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,If I blast him, I'll win the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.23,0:17:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And he'll be gone forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.45,0:17:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,One attack and I can finally\Nmove on with my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.47,0:17:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I got something for you, Mai.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.43,0:17:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Up high!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.07,0:17:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.81,0:17:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right, Mai. I'm right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.95,0:17:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.55,0:17:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Saving your life, Mike.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.37,0:17:47.20,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.28,0:17:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,See you around.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.33,0:17:49.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.29,0:17:52.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.20,0:17:53.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You win.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.47,0:17:59.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.75,0:18:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.09,0:18:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I never attacked, so you\Ndidn't lose the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.99,0:18:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'm too exhausted to finish.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.69,0:18:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't let the Orikalkos\Ntake you away, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.63,0:18:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too late for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.57,0:18:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I already lost a duel, so\Nthere's no turning back.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.93,0:18:26.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just glad that if one of us had to lose\Nour soul, it didn't have to be you, Mai.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.55,0:18:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't say that!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.27,0:18:34.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Mai, that was one of the greatest\Nduels I ever fought. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.57,0:18:39.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.67,0:18:42.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.09,0:18:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,She's been set free!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.09,0:18:48.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, but what's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.27,0:18:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems Miss Valentine\Nhas served her purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.53,0:18:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no! What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.75,0:18:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it Joey?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.97,0:18:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid so.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.71,0:19:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What's up with Pegasus?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.01,0:19:15.48,Default,,0,0,0,,There must be some kind of\Nglitch in the holographic image.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.83,0:19:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey! Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.77,0:19:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Snap out of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.89,0:19:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,This is all my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.07,0:19:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I was angry and confused, and I\Nblamed all my loneliness on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.47,0:19:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,So I tried to get rid of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.69,0:19:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I be so selfish?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.27,0:19:37.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the only one who\Never cared about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.87,0:19:43.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the closest friend I ever\Nhad, and how did I repay you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.77,0:19:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,By leaving you for a madman\Nwho promised me power.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.51,0:19:52.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make him regret the day\Nhe ever met my Valentine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.17,0:20:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The only way to fix this is\Nto meet darts face to face.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.21,0:20:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Here goes nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.29,0:20:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Cave Darts, is that you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.87,0:20:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess again, Mai.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.77,0:20:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.68,0:20:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.13,0:20:43.57,Default,,0,0,0,,No way. What happened?\NHe lost the duel. Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.65,0:20:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,does that mean yes his\Nsoul belongs to darts now
